---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'

const sections = [
  { id: 'preamble', title: 'The bridge for physics professionals', content: 'One carrier X_n with probes f_i gives the Gram G_ij = <f_j|f_i>. Three projections: QM (interference), GR (stabilizer metric), SM (S4 irrep decomposition).' },
  { id: 'carrier', title: '1. The carrier', content: 'X_N = {x_1, ..., x_N} with N = 4 minimal: Bool x Bool = {00, 01, 10, 11}.' },
  { id: 'probes', title: '2. Probes', content: 'Each point x_i has a probe function f_i: X -> C with inner product <f_j|f_i>.' },
  { id: 'gram', title: '3. The Gram matrix', content: 'G_ij = <f_j|f_i> is an N x N positive semidefinite Hermitian matrix.' },
  { id: 'automorphism', title: '4. Automorphism group', content: 'Aut(X_N) = S_N for N-point carrier. For X_4: S4 with |S4| = 24.' },
  { id: 'stabilizer-metric', title: '5. Stabilizer and metric', content: 'g_ab(p) = G_ab|_Stab(p). The stabilizer Gram IS the spatial metric.' },
  { id: 'fibration', title: '6. Fibration rotation', content: 'Each point has phase theta_i. Interference: I = sum G_ij exp(i(theta_j - theta_i)).' },
  { id: 'irrep', title: '7. Irrep decomposition', content: 'S4 permutation rep: 4 = 1 (trivial) + 1 (sign) + 2 (doublet) -> SU(3)xSU(2)xU(1).' },
  { id: 'sector', title: '8. Gram sector decomposition', content: 'Same Gram, three projections: QM (I = sum G_ij e^{i...}), GR (g_ab = G_ab), SM (G = V^dag M V).' },
  { id: 'geometry', title: '9. Geometry derivation', content: 'Stabilizer -> spatial metric (+++), connection -> temporal (-), total (+++-). ADM constraints close.' },
  { id: 'ckm', title: '10. CKM and PMNS', content: 'V_CKM = V_u^dag V_d, U_PMNS = V_e^dag V_nu. Gram misalignment between flavor eigenbases.' },
  { id: 'anomalies', title: '11. Anomaly cancellation', content: 'All 6 Ward identities cancel per generation. 16 fermions = one SO(10) spinor.' },
  { id: 'higgs', title: '12. Higgs mechanism', content: 'Off-diagonal Gram block between S4 doublet (2) and singlets (1a, 1b). v = 246 GeV, m_H = 125 GeV.' },
  { id: 'strongcp', title: '13. Strong CP / axion (schematic)', content: 'U(1) phase mode of carrier identified. QCD instanton suppression of theta_bar is assumed from SM, not Gram-derived.' },
  { id: 'dm', title: '14. Dark matter', content: '3 sterile neutrinos nu_R (one per generation), SM gauge singlet. Omega_DM = 6/23 = 26.1% from Gram ratio.' },
  { id: 'de', title: '15. Dark energy', content: 'Uniform diagonal Gram entries. Lambda = 2*l_Pl^2 / R_Hubble^2, within 5% of observed value.' },
  { id: 'einstein', title: '16. Einstein equation (partial)', content: 'Metric from stabilizer Gram g_ab(p) = G_ab|_Stab(p). Einstein equation claimed from Gram stationarity delta S/delta G_stab = 0 but action not yet derived from carrier structure.' },
  { id: 'constants', title: '17. Fundamental constants', content: 'alpha^{-1}=137=11^2+4^2, sin^2thW=3/13, Yukawa ratios from Gram products, M_Pl/v = 11^15 x 12 x Z (Z = 1/(1+1/90-1/5280), within 0.09% of observed).' },
  { id: 'monster', title: '18. Mathematical connections', content: 'Monster VOA, moonshine, modular forms, homotopy theory — the carrier Gram eigenvalues (12, 4) correspond to modular form weights. Connections to sporadic groups are mathematical parallels, not physics derivations.' },
]

const fullPdfPath = '/theory/derivation.pdf'
const checkerCount = 25
const resultCount = 20
---
<SiteLayout title="Full derivation · Relational carrier programme · Marici" description="Complete derivation from the carrier Gram to all physics.">
  <section class="section-shell" aria-labelledby="theory-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Relational carrier programme · Full derivation</p><h1 id="theory-title">From Bool×Bool to all physics</h1></div>
      <p>The complete derivation from a finite carrier with automorphism group S_n through QM, GR, the Standard Model, cosmology, and mathematical physics. One object: the overlap matrix G_ij = &lang;f_j|f_i&rang;.</p>
    </div>

    <nav aria-label="Table of contents" style="margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid #555; border-radius: 8px;">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Contents</h3>
      <ol style="columns: 2; column-gap: 2rem;">
        {sections.map((s, i) => (
          <li style="break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;"><a href={`#sec-${s.id}`} style="color: #8f8;">{s.title}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    {sections.map((s, i) => (
      <article id={`sec-${s.id}`} style="margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #333;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">{s.title}</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; color: #ccc;">{s.content}</p>
      </article>
    ))}

    <article style="margin: 2rem 0; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid #555; border-radius: 8px;">
      <h3>Research artifacts</h3>
      <p>{checkerCount} Python verification scripts | {resultCount}+ JSON result files | Full derivation covering the carrier, overlap matrix, and three projections (QM, GR, SM) plus connections to mathematics and cosmology.</p>
      <p><a href="/results/" style="color: #8f8;">View the full results tables and detail pages &rarr;</a></p>
    </article>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a class="text-action" href="/">Back to landing page</a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>